    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Warm AIHA relapsing after or refractory to glucocorticoids: rituximab 375 mg/m2 IV wkly for 4 wks (alternatives 1000 mg on days 1 and 15, or 100 mg wkly x4)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Warm AIHA, refractory cases: IVIG, immunosuppressants (azathioprine, mycophenolate, cyclophosphamide), splenectomy; IVIG has given temp control of less severe but uncontrolled hemolysis."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Cold agglutinin dz: ⍉cold; rituximab, sometimes w bendamustine; glucocorticoids have limited effect and shouldn't be used."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Sutimlimab (classical complement inhibitor) for severe or Sxtomatic cold agglutinin anemia; vaccinate against encapsulated bacteria >= 2 wks b4."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
